strings (\"U10 D5\"). For class 2, numeric is fine. Let me use 2.\n\nActually wait — accuracy_classes[] in recommendation schema. I'll put [2].\n\n- q2_q1_ratio: 1.6 (dimensionless)\n- q4_q3_ratio: 1.25\n- water_pressure_class: \"MAP16\" (string)\n- pressure_loss_class: \"Δp63\" (string)\n- reverse_flow: \"Not designed to measure\" — it's a text characteristic. Include as string value.\n- environmental_class: \"O\"\n- maximum_admissible_pressure: 1.6 MPa\n- orientation_limitation: \"H (horizontal position with indicating device at top)\" — value string \"H\" plus description? I'll do value \"H\" and maybe a note. Keep value: \"H (horizontal position with the indicating device at top)\"? Cleaner: value \"H\". Hmm the orientation limitation cell: \"H (for horizontal position with the indicating device at top)\". I'll record orientation: {value: \"H\"} and orientation_description separately? Simpler: value \"H\". I'll add attribute orientation: \"H\" and orientation_limitation: \"H (horizontal position with the indicating device at top)\"? Redundant. I'll do one: orientation_limitation value \"H\" — losing the explanation. Or keep full string. I'll keep value: \"H\", and add \"orientation\": \"Horizontal position with indicating device at top\"? Meh. Just value: \"H\". Actually the marking requires \"Letter H↑\". I'll do orientation: \"H (horizontal, indicating device at top)\". One attribute: orientation, value \"H\". Fine.\n\nLet me structure type_level:\n- measuring_principle: \"Woltmann, dry dial\"\n- accuracy_class: 2\n- mpe_lower_flowrate_zone: {min:-5,max:5} %\n- water_pressure_class: \"MAP16\"\n- pressure_loss_class: \"Δp63\"\n- reverse_flow: \"Not designed to measure\"\n- environmental_class: \"O\"\n- maximum_admissible_pressure: 1.6 MPa\n- orientation: \"H\"\n- connection_type: \"Flange\"\n- flow_profile_sensitivity_class: \"U10 D5\"\n- flow_conditioner: \"no\" → value false? \"no\" string. I'll use \"no\".\n- q2_q1_ratio: 1.6\n- q4_q3_ratio: 1.25\n\nStructured values need {value, unit_symbol, unit_id} shape. For string values, unit_symbol null.\n\nFor \"value\" key each characteristic value is the object. E.g.:\n\n\"measuring_principle\": {\"value\": \"Woltmann, dry dial\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}\n\nShould footnote_markers be present always? Rule 7: record marker when referenced. I'll include footnote_markers: [] or omit when empty. I'll omit when empty to reduce noise. The shape example shows footnote_markers present; but rule 8 says omit what's absent. I'll omit empty ones.\n\nComponents:\n[\n  {\n    \"role\": \"indicating device\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"LYG\", \"GB\"],\n    \"alternatives\": \"OR\",\n    \"characteristics\": {\n      \"LYG\": \"Plastic Calculator (dry)\",\n      \"GB\": \"Copper Can Calculator (super dry)\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"reed impulse transmitter (optional, for remote reading)\",\n    \"type_designations\": [],\n    \"alternatives\": null\n  }\n]\n\nHmm, characteristics{} for components — free-form. Maybe better:\ncomponents[0]: role \"indicating device (dry dial)\", type_designations [\"LYG – Plastic Calculator\", \"GB – Copper Can Calculator\"], alternatives \"OR\".\ncomponents[1]: role \"measurement unit\" — description mentions interchangeable wet measurement unit with adjusting device. Probably skip.\ncomponents[1]: role \"reed impulse transmitter\", note optional. I'll include with type_designations [] and characteristics {optional: true}? Keep simple: role \"Reed impulse transmitter (optional, for remote reading)\".\n\nAlso description field for certified_type: I'll summarize:\n\"Horizontal Woltmann water meter with cast iron body with connecting flanges and interchangeable wet measurement unit with adjusting device; dry (Plastic Calculator – LYG) or super dry (Copper Can Calculator – GB) mechanical indicating device with six drums and three rotary pointers, or seven drums and two rotary pointers; optional reed impulse transmitter for remote reading; horizontal installation only with indicating device at top.\"\n\nCategory: \"Water meter\". The certificate title says \"water meter – Woltmann\". I'll use \"Water meter\".\n\ntype_designations: [\"LXLC\", \"LXSG-20\"]? The LXSG-20 mention... Let me re-read: \"The water meters types LXSG-20 shall be clearly and indelibly marked with the following information (Figure 2):\" — Figure 2 shows \"LXLC-50\" dial. So LXSG-20 is inconsistent; likely an error in the original cert (possibly copied from another cert). To be faithful I'll include both in type_designations. Hmm... but this could pollute. The instruction says \"all type/model identifiers mentioned\". I'll include \"LXSG-20\". Actually, let me reconsider — risk: downstream user searches for model LXSG-20 in a cert that certifies LXLC. It IS mentioned. Faithful extraction includes it. I'll include it. Hmm, but wait: it might confuse. The safest is include both — extraction shouldn't editorialize. Include.\n\nModel designations in type_designations too? \"LXLC-50\" etc. are model numbers — they go in models[]. type_designations: [\"LXLC\", \"LXSG-20\"]. Fine.\n\nRecommendation:\n{\n  \"id\": \"R49\",\n  \"edition\": 2013,\n  \"scheme\": \"A\",\n  \"accuracy_classes\": [2]\n}\n\nWait — \"OIML R 49 Edition (year): 2013\". The recommendation is R 49 (Water meters...). edition: 2013.\n\nCertificate oiml_issuer_id: omit.\n\nNow dates: date_issued: The certificate signing date is 31 January 2023; revision history \"Addition 0, 31 January 2023, Issuing certificate\". So date_issued \"2023-01-31\".\n\nPage_total: 10.\n\nProject number: not present. Omit.\n\nLet me now also decide whether to include \"resolution of the device for rapid testing\" — it's \"-\", empty. Omit per rule 8.\n\nReed switch power supply, K-factor: \"-\" → omit.\n\nPower supply details all \"-\" → omit (it's mechanical, no power).\n\nSoftware version \"-\": omit.\n\nEUT testing requirements Category/Case \"-\": omit.\n\nNow let me carefully re-verify numbers from tables:\n\nPage 3-4 GB table (LXLC-50, 65, 80):\n- Dial plate design: GB, GB, GB\n- Nominal diameter: 50, 65, 80\n- Q3/Q1: 40, 50, 40, 50, 40, 50\n- Q2/Q1: 1.6\n- Q4/Q3: 1.25\n- Measuring principle: Woltmann, dry dial\n- Accuracy class: 2\n- MPE lower: ±5 %\n- MPE upper: ±2% ≤30°C, ±3% >30°C\n- Temperature class: T30;T50 | T90 | T30;T50 | T90 | T30;T50 | T90\n- Water pressure class: MAP16\n- Pressure loss class: Δp63\n- Reverse flow: Not designed to measure\n- Environmental class: O\n- Max admissible temp [°C]: 50 or 90\n- Max admissible pressure [MPa]: 1.6\n- Orientation limitation: H\n- Indicating range [m³]: 9 999 999 ×3\n- Resolution of indicating device [m³]: 0.002 ×3\n- Connection type: Flange\n- Min straight inlet [mm]: 500, 650, 800\n- Min straight outlet [mm]: 250, 325, 400\n- Flow profile sensitivity class: U10 D5\n- Flow conditioner: no\n- Length [mm]: 200, 200, 225\n\nPage 5 (GB, LXLC-100, 150, 200):\n- Nominal diameter: 100, 150, 200\n- Q3/Q1: 40, 50, 40, 50, 40, 50\n- Q2/Q1 1.6, Q4/Q3 1.25, class 2, MAP16, Δp63, env O\nPage 6 continuation:\n- Max admissible temp: 50 or 90; MAP 1.6 MPa\n- Indicating range: 9 999 999 | 99 999 999 | 99 999 999\n- Resolution: 0.002 | 0.02 | 0.02\n- Inlet: 1000, 1250, 1500\n- Outlet: 500, 625, 750\n- Length: 250, 250, 300\n\nPage 7 (LYG, all six):\n- Dial plate: LYG ×6\n- Nominal diameter: 50, 65, 80, 100, 150, 200\n- Q3/Q1: 40 (all)\n- Temperature class: T30; T50 (all)\n- Indicating range: 999 999 ×6\n- Resolution: 0.0005, 0.0005, 0.0005, 0.0005, 0.002, 0.002\n- Inlet: 500, 650, 800, 1000, 1250, 1500\n- Outlet: 250, 325, 400, 500, 625, 750\n- Length: 200, 200, 225, 250, 250, 300\n\nPage 8 flowrates table: as listed above. Note LXLC-50/65 Q1 R40 = 1.250 → odd but as stated.\n\nNow, indicating range: \"9 999 999\" = 9,999,999 = 9999999. \"99 999 999\" = 99999999. \"999 999\" = 999999.\n\nResolution GB-150/200: 0.02. LYG 50-100: 0.0005; 150/200: 0.002.\n\nNow mark whether temp classes for GB models with R40: T30;T50 — meaning either T30 or T50 variant available. So condition mapping temperature_class ratio 40 → \"T30; T50\" (both possible), 50 → \"T90\". And max admissible temperature: for T30/T50 → 50°C, T90 → 90°C. The cert \"50 or 90\" supports that.\n\nNow, mark whether LYG supports ratio 50: The LYG table shows only Q3/Q1: 40. So LYG: [40].\n\nAlso GB table on page 3 header shows model number LXLC – 50 etc. with dial plate GB. Good.\n\nNow description of marking section — skip (not characteristics). Could note in description? Not needed.\n\nLet me now think about \"number of drums/pointers\" — description mentions two register configurations: six drums + three pointers, or seven drums + two pointers. These correspond to LYG/GB? Not explicitly mapped. Keep in description only.\n\nNow build the JSON.\n\nTop-level:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-2023.01\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"page_total\": 10,\n    \"member_state\": \"Czech Republic\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2023-01-31\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"Czech Metrology Institute\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\"Okružní 31\", \"638 00 Brno\", \"Czech Republic\"],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"Jan Kalandra\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Cixi Cidong Flow Instrument Co., Ltd\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"No. 148, Longzhen Road, Longshan Industrial Park\", \"315 311 Ningbo, Zhejiang\", \"China\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"manufacturers\": [ same ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"LXLC\", \"LXSG-20\"],\n    \"module_designation\": \"Not applicable\",\n    \"description\": \"...\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {...},\n  \"components\": [...],\n  \"characteristics\": {...},\n  \"matrix_tables\": [...],\n  \"recommendation\": {...},\n  \"test_reports\": [...],\n  \"revision_history\": [...]\n}\n\nAddress parsing: \"No. 148, Longzhen Road, Longshan Industrial Park, 315 311 Ningbo, Zhejiang (China)\". Split: [\"No. 148, Longzhen Road, Longshan Industrial Park\", \"315 311 Ningbo, Zhejiang\", \"China\"]. Keep \"(China)\" → \"China\".\n\nDescription: \"Horizontal Woltmann water meter consisting of a cast iron body with connecting flanges, an interchangeable wet measurement unit with adjusting device, and a dry mechanical indicating device (Plastic Calculator – LYG) or super dry mechanical indicating device (Copper Can Calculator – GB). Indicating device formed by numbered rollers with six drums and three rotary pointers, or seven drums and two rotary pointers. Optionally equipped with a reed impulse transmitter for remote reading. Installed in horizontal position only with the indicating device at the top.\"\n\nmodule_designation: The form has \"-\" → \"Not applicable\". Schema: \"Analog load cell\" | \"Not applicable\" | null. Use \"Not applicable\".\n\nModel family:\n\n\"model_family\": {\n  \"family_name\": \"LXLC\",\n  \"models\": [\n    {\"model_id\": \"LXLC-50-GB\", \"label\": \"LXLC – 50, dial plate GB\", \"attributes\": {\"nominal_diameter\": 50, \"dial_plate_design\": \"GB\", \"calculator_type\": \"Copper Can Calculator (super dry)\", \"available_q3_q1_ratios\": [40, 50]}},\n    {\"model_id\": \"LXLC-50-LYG\", \"label\": \"LXLC – 50, dial plate LYG\", \"attributes\": {\"nominal_diameter\": 50, \"dial_plate_design\": \"LYG\", \"calculator_type\": \"Plastic Calculator (dry)\", \"available_q3_q1_ratios\": [40]}},\n    ... 65, 80, 100, 150, 200\n  ]\n}\n\n12 model entries.\n\ncharacteristics.model_level:\n\n1. {\n  \"attribute\": \"nominal_diameter\",\n  \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"model\": \"LXLC-50-GB\", \"value\": 50},\n    {\"model\": \"LXLC-50-LYG\", \"value\": 50},\n    {\"model\": \"LXLC-65-GB\", \"value\": 65},\n    {\"model\": \"LXLC-65-LYG\", \"value\": 65},\n    {\"model\": \"LXLC-80-GB\", \"value\": 80},\n    {\"model\": \"LXLC-80-LYG\", \"value\": 80},\n    {\"model\": \"LXLC-100-GB\", \"value\"